      "statement": "create_resource_fork requires that the original resource is not itself a fork (is_fork must be False), is_public, and allow_forks is True; it creates a new PubResource with is_fork=True and allow_forks=False (preventing fork-of-fork chains), inheriting subject_id, target_id, education_level, and difficulty_level from the original while title/description come from the PubResourceCreateFork input, and records a PubResourceFork row linking original_id to forked_id and the forking author_id.",
